-- title:
--   Every element of the localized node ring is congruent to a constant
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime with $q\neq 2$, let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, let $k$ be a field of characteristic $q$ and $\mathrm{red}\colon A\to k$ a ring homomorphism. Let $K$ be an intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q$ that is finite over $\mathbb Q$, write $A_0=\mathrm{coeffSubring}\,A\,K=A\cap K$ for the intersection of $A$ with $K$ inside $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, and let $\mathrm{red}_0=\mathrm{redRestrict}$ be the restriction of $\mathrm{red}$ to $A_0$. Let $l\in k$ satisfy $l^{q^2}=l$ and let $y\in A_0$ be an element with $\mathrm{red}_0(y)=l$. Let $\Lambda=\mathrm{lambdaEval}$ be the ring homomorphism $\mathrm{MvPolynomial}(\mathrm{Fin}\ 2)\,A_0\to\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,\overline{\mathbb Q}$ sending a coefficient to the corresponding constant series and the two variables to $\mathrm{lambdaModC}$ and to its $q$-th $q$-expansion $\mathrm{lambdaNModC}$, and let $S=\mathrm{lambdaLocalizedAtPoint}$ be the subring of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,\overline{\mathbb Q}$ consisting of those $f$ for which there are polynomials $r,s$ with $f\cdot\Lambda(s)=\Lambda(r)$ and $\mathrm{pointEval}(s)=\mathrm{eval}_{(\mathrm{red}_0;\,l,\,l^q)}(s)\neq 0$. Assume $S$ is a local ring. Then for every $z\in S$ there is $o\in A_0$ such that $z-\Lambda(C\,o)$, the difference of $z$ and the constant Laurent series attached to $o$, lies in the maximal ideal of $S$.
--
--   The assertion is that the composite $A_0\to S\to S/\mathfrak m_S$ is surjective, i.e. the residue field of the localization of the level-$q$ lambda ring at the supersingular-type point $(l,l^q)$ is generated by constants from $A\cap K$. It is used in the construction of the subring identification with an adic completion attached to stabilizers, `exists_subring_adicCompletion_ringEquiv_eqLocus_of_stabilizer_of_eq_zero_or_eq_1728`.
-- source:
